a MN.ttc) normal normal 400 normal>) = 10.05\r\n2021-03-10 19:16:56.454 findfont: Matching sans\\-serif:style=normal:variant=normal:weight=normal:stretch=normal:size=12.0 to DejaVu Sans ('/opt/anaconda3/lib/python3.8/site-packages/matplotlib/mpl-data/fonts/ttf/DejaVuSans.ttf') with score of 0.050000.\r\n2021-03-10 19:16:56.454 findfont: score(<Font 'Menlo' (Menlo.ttc) normal normal 400 normal>) = 10.05\r\n2021-03-10 19:16:56.454 findfont: Matching sans\\-serif:style=normal:variant=normal:weight=normal:stretch=normal:size=12.0 to DejaVu Sans ('/opt/anaconda3/lib/python3.8/site-packages/matplotlib/mpl-data/fonts/ttf/DejaVuSans.ttf') with score of 0.050000.\r\n2021-03-10 19:16:56.454 findfont: score(<Font '.SF Compact Text' (SFCompactText-SemiboldItalic.otf) italic normal 600 normal>) = 11.24\r\n2021-03-10 19:16:56.455 findfont: score(<Font 'Bangla MN' (Bangla MN.ttc) normal normal 400 normal>) = 10.05\r\n2021-03-10 19:16:56.455 findfont: Matching sans\\-serif:style=normal:variant=normal:weight=normal:stretch=normal:size=12.0 to DejaVu Sans ('/opt/anaconda3/lib/python3.8/site-packages/matplotlib/mpl-data/fonts/ttf/DejaVuSans.ttf') with score of 0.050000.\r\npython(48519,0x700017765000) malloc: Incorrect checksum for freed object 0x7f85dc7ab018: probably modified after being freed.\r\nCorrupt value: 0x70001b0014007b04\r\npython(48519,0x700017765000) malloc: *** set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug\r\nzsh: abort      streamlit run main.py --logger.level=debug\r\n```\r\n(fitting into the above error message where its talking about fonts).\r\n\r\nI checked and it seems like this doesn't happen when I use a very simple app (just `import streamlit as st; st.write(\"test\")) and I am now wondering if it is because I have to read/write to a data file. I tried refreshing the data file externally and then it runs again further making me think this.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/issues/comments/7959487